	'k095f79e4' => 'We keep booking straightforward, personal, and transparent, with all room rates including daily breakfast and farm activities. Plan your family stay above the old hay barn between 1 February and 20 December.',
	'k09b52760' => 'Dairy Farming Since 1962',
	'k0afcd5e9' => 'Calves bottle-fed, hens’ eggs collected, hay forked down — with Mateo and Rosa.',
	'k0b4b9f4f' => 'Guests are invited to assist with five primary chores: walking out to bring the milking herd in at 05:30, bottle-feeding our twelve calves at 10:00, collecting fresh eggs from Rosa\'s hen coops, forking sweet hay down from the lofts with Mateo, and shaking cream into fresh butter with Lukas Brandt. Safety remains our highest priority across the farmyard. Closed shoes or sturdy boots are mandatory at all times. Children under eight years old must be accompanied by an adult guardian, and visitors never enter the bull pen. Children never operate farm machinery, tractors, or electrical equipment.',
