	'k146cac7d' => 'A FARM DAY',
	'k14c14aa2' => 'Staying with us means living in step with the actual pace of farm life rather than a staged display. Guests sleep above the hay barn where swallows nest in the rafters, waking early to the sound of hooves heading to the milking parlour. With 48 cows in the fields and five regular times structuring each day, there is always purposeful work underway. Whether you are forking hay with Mateo or resting under the walnut tree in the afternoon sun, you share in the quiet continuity of sixty years on Larkfield Valley.',
	'k14c3ebdd' => 'Ilse replies within 24 hours to confirm dates and send a secure 30% deposit link.',
	'k15738e5a' => 'Shake cream into rich butter in glass jars with Lukas.',
	'k16919e10' => 'Larkfield Hollow Farm has operated as a dedicated dairy farm since 1962, set amidst seventy hectares of rolling hill pastures in Larkfield Valley. In 2014, we carefully converted the loft of the old timber hay barn into four family guest rooms, creating a place where travelers can experience genuine agricultural life. Today, the farm is home to 48 milking cows—a hardy herd of Holstein and Brown Swiss crosses—alongside 12 young calves, a flock of free-range hens, and two friendly yard goats. We keep the rhythm of the farm honest, seasonal, and welcoming.',
	'k176645b1' => 'Collect eggs',
	'k1885c0c5' => 'Each morning at 07:00, Ilse Ferreira welcomes guests to a hearty farm breakfast in the barn kitchen, included with every room reservation. The spread features fresh milk drawn that morning, golden butter churned on-site, freshly gathered eggs, and crusty loaves baked in the oven. At 13:00, following the butter-making session with Lukas Brandt in the dairy room, guests can assemble a meadow picnic basket. Packed with fresh bread, sliced cheese, churned butter, and fruit, baskets can be carried into the pastures for a quiet family lunch among the clover.',
