	'k9252b8ff' => 'Butter session',
	'k928c75fa' => 'In 2014, we converted the upper floor of our timber hay barn into four spacious guest rooms for visiting families. Guests sleep under exposed wooden rafters, wake to the soft lowing of forty-eight cows in the meadows below, and join directly in the authentic daily work of the homestead.',
	'k92c594f9' => 'Farmer, third generation',
	'k92dac2cc' => 'Help on the Farm',
	'k93464b79' => 'We provide',
	'k95884b52' => 'Summer',
	'k95ef7c3a' => 'Guests have access to a well-equipped shared kitchenette in the barn for preparing light meals, hot drinks, and children\'s snacks between farm activities. A laundry facility with washing machines and drying racks is also available for muddy clothes after chores, and travel cots can be provided upon advance request. Every reservation includes our farm breakfast at 07:00 and all daily farm activities. We require a minimum stay of two nights. A 30% deposit is required to confirm your reservation, and we provide free cancellation up to 14 days before your scheduled arrival date.',
	'k9734c1e3' => 'Sleeps 2 adults + 2 children',
	'k984ceac1' => 'Included',
	'k9868826d' => 'At any time of year, we look after twelve calves in the airy straw pens beside the main barn. Because calving follows the natural cycle of the herd, births occur throughout our February to December season, though we can\'t promise a birth during any specific stay. When a calf is born, guests are welcome to observe quietly under the supervision of Noor or Tomas. Mateo Ferreira oversees daily calf care, guiding children as they mix warm milk and hold nursing bottles for the young calves during morning chores.',
	'k9883e394' => 'Book a stay',
	'k992fac80' => 'Milking morning, farm chores, butter session',
	'k9a0415ce' => 'Because Larkfield Hollow Farm is an active dairy enterprise, sensible outdoor clothing is necessary. Sturdy closed shoes or rubber boots are strictly required for entering the parlour, cattle sheds, and calf pens; sandals are not allowed in working zones. We recommend bringing comfortable clothes that can tolerate mud, layers for cool valley mornings, and waterproof jackets. Chores proceed in all weather, moving indoors to dry barns when rain falls.',
	'k9a8ab6a5' => 'The morning begins at 05:30 with Milking. Guests can walk to the parlour with Tomas Ferreira, where children aged five and older are invited to help bring the cows in from the pasture and hold the yard gate. Participation is entirely optional for those who prefer to sleep in. At 07:00, everyone gathers in the barn kitchen for Breakfast. The table is laden with fresh milk from that morning\'s milking, sweet farm butter, eggs gathered from the hen run, and crusty loaves of warm bread freshly baked in the oven.',
	'k9acada61' => 'What are your seasonal dates, check-in times, and desk hours?',
	'k9bfc64b6' => 'We offer four spacious guest rooms designed specifically for families. The Orchard Room sleeps two adults and one child for €165 per night, offering gentle morning light. The Swallow Room accommodates two adults and two children at €185 per night, featuring views across the open yard. For larger families, the Hayloft Room sleeps two adults and three children with a dedicated bunk alcove for €210 per night. Finally, the Rafters Suite accommodates two families or up to six guests across generous interconnected rooms for €245 per night. Every room is furnished with comfortable beds, exposed rafters, and linen bedding.',
	'k9c01afe2' => 'See the rooms →',
	'k9cb0517e' => 'Can we expect to see a calf being born during our visit?',
	'k9e1c1714' => 'Valley mornings are cool at 05:30.',
	'k9e833aaa' => 'Makiba Farmstay opens for guests from 1 February through 20 December each year. The farm is closed to guests from 21 December through 31 January for winter maintenance and resting pastures. Check-in takes place between 15:00 and 18:00, followed by an introductory farm walk with Tomas Ferreira at 17:00. Check-out on your departure morning is by 11:00. Our booking desk answers calls and emails daily between 08:00 and 19:00.',
	'k9ecd0fe6' => 'Rooms open',
