	'kb0974eab' => 'Calves and tractor',
	'kb18e66b4' => 'Winter',
	'kb2777f11' => 'Families often find that everyday farm routines create lasting memories. The Okafor family, visiting with their two children aged six and nine for three nights in April, stayed up into the night for a calf born at 04:10, proudly naming the newborn heifer Biscuit. Grete spent a week in the Hayloft Room during August with her young grandsons, who took charge of the hen coop rounds every morning with Rosa. The Laurent twins, aged seven, experienced their first pre-dawn milking with Tomas and now ask their parents for a milking holiday every single year.',
	'kb311a3fe' => 'Morning',
	'kb3274b8e' => 'Life here follows the steady turn of the seasons and the farm clock, from dawn milking in the parlour to late dinners in the yard. With forty-eight milking cows, twelve calves, free-ranging hens, and two goats, the farm offers children and parents an honest, restorative countryside stay.',
	'kb34fe310' => 'Farm-day times',
	'kb45ecf28' => 'Four times each year, we send a seasonal letter from Larkfield Valley reflecting on life across the farm. Read quiet news from the pastures, dairy herd, and barn kitchen.',
	'kb4c3ae8f' => 'Larkfield Hollow Farm is located along Weald Lane in the heart of Larkfield Valley. We welcome guests from 1 February through 20 December for quiet family farmstays.',
