	'kb84b7c77' => 'cows',
	'kb8a24089' => 'At 10:00, morning Chores begin as guests join Mateo and Rosa to bottle-feed the twelve calves, collect newly laid eggs from the coop, and fork fragrant hay into the mangers. At 13:00, Lukas Brandt hosts the Butter &amp; picnic session in the dairy room, where children shake jars of fresh cream into yellow butter before packing a basket to enjoy in the meadow. The day concludes at 18:30 with our evening Barbecue under the walnut tree on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Saturdays, prepared by cook Ama Owusu for €22 per adult and €11 per child aged four to twelve.',
	'kb8b039f9' => 'Tue, Thu, Sat · 18:30',
	'kba6580e6' => 'Yes, children are warmly invited to participate alongside our family. Children aged five and older can help Tomas bring the cows in for milking at 05:30 and hold the parlour gates. At 10:00, children help bottle-feed the twelve calves and collect eggs with Rosa. Children under eight must be accompanied by an adult guardian at all times, sturdy closed footwear is mandatory, and guests never enter the bull pen.',
	'kba7311ab' => 'Back down the lane each late afternoon for the evening milking.',
	'kbbaff128' => 'Contact',
	'kbc47fc33' => 'Orchard Room',
	'kbcae1e48' => 'The harvest from Rosa’s garden and the orchard.',
	'kbcc254b5' => 'Phone',
	'kbe4db61e' => 'The people of the farm',
	'kbf7eb013' => 'Shake butter in jars in the dairy room with Lukas, then a picnic basket for the meadow.',
	'kbf9ebac9' => 'A quiet rest while the farm is closed to guests.',
	'kbfbf8295' => 'Lukas Brandt',
	'kbfeea4c4' => '13:00 · Included',
	'kc1814743' => 'A basket of bread, cheese, butter and fruit to carry to the pasture.',
	'kc20daf06' => 'Dairy room',
	'kc24d00a7' => '05:30 to 18:30',
	'kc2507511' => 'The Family and Farm Team',
	'kc2f5ca3b' => 'Room Rates and Inclusions',
	'kc313ab08' => 'Fires the grill on barbecue nights.',
	'kc430080e' => 'From our dairy and kitchen garden',
	'kc5384a66' => 'Rooms are €165 to €245 a night with the farm breakfast included; the evening barbecue is €22 per adult and €11 per child. Minimum stay 2 nights. 30% deposit to confirm; free cancellation up to 14 days before arrival.',
	'kc596d725' => 'Hectares of pasture',
	'kc5a43fbf' => 'Our four family rooms are set directly above the historic timber hay barn, looking out across the farmyard and green hill pastures. Every stay includes our hearty farm breakfast, hands-on daily chores, and access to shared barn amenities.',
	'kc7da4b85' => 'After the butter session',
	'kc7e4d509' => 'When are evening barbecues held, and what do they cost?',
	'kc880f619' => 'Two families, 6 guests',
	'kc89d2d66' => 'With 48 milking cows and twelve calves on site, births occur regularly across our open season from February to December. Because calving follows the natural cycle of the herd, we can\'t promise a birth during any particular visit. If a birth does take place while you are staying with us, guests are welcome to observe quietly alongside herd manager Noor Haddad and Tomas Ferreira, just as the Okafor family did with Biscuit.',
	'kcbade20b' => 'Our farm is sustained by a small, dedicated group of family members and skilled hands. Tomas Ferreira is a third-generation farmer who manages daily farm work and leads the 05:30 morning milking. His wife, Ilse Ferreira, looks after the guest rooms, coordinates bookings, and prepares the breakfast table. Their nineteen-year-old son, Mateo, feeds the calves and handles tractor work across the fields. Tomas\'s mother, Rosa, tends the flock of hens and cultivates the kitchen garden. They are joined by herd manager Noor Haddad, who oversees herd health in the parlour; Lukas Brandt, who crafts butter and fresh cheese in the dairy room; and evening cook Ama Owusu, who prepares yard barbecues.',
	'kcc465208' => 'Rafters Suite',
	'kcc58a1f8' => 'Our dairy herd of 48 milking cows and 12 calves is the living foundation of Larkfield Hollow Farm. We manage our animals with patience and care, letting them graze open pastures through the warmer months.',
	'kcd209aa5' => 'The farm letter',
	'kce8ae9da' => 'Email',
	'kcefc4f7c' => 'Family',
	'kd0c94905' => '“The Okafor family (two children, 6 and 9) arrived for 3 nights in April, stayed up for a calf born at 04:10; the children named her Biscuit. They still talk about holding the torch and watching her first steps in the straw.”',
	'kd22b702b' => 'what families help with',
	'kd3e697b6' => 'From the loft, with Mateo.',
	'kd50fcee5' => 'Guests never enter it.',
	'kd56c36ba' => 'Email: <a href="mailto:stay@makibafarm.example">stay@makibafarm.example</a>',
	'kd7887647' => 'Makiba Farmstay is a working dairy farm in Larkfield Valley, welcoming guests to four family rooms built above our historic hay barn. Since 1962, three generations of our family have cared for the herd, the pastures, and this land.',
	'kd853d95e' => 'Leads the 05:30 milking and walks the new guests round the yard at 17:00.',
	'kd8addef2' => 'Hayloft Room',
	'kd9af136b' => 'The farm',
	'kd9d403c2' => 'Rooms Above the Hay Barn',
	'kdc660812' => 'Two double beds, generous interconnected rooms and a reading nook by the window, made for two families travelling together.',
	'kdca78c60' => 'Hens and kitchen garden',
	'kdccee3b1' => 'Walk to the parlour with Tomas; children from age 5 help bring the cows in and hold the gate. Optional.',
	'kdcf94eae' => 'A waterproof coat',
	'kddc2c2fa' => 'Ask for dates by form or by email. Ilse replies within 24 hours with a 30% deposit link; check-in is 15:00–18:00 and Tomas walks arriving families round the farm at 17:00.',
	'kde6516a8' => 'Phone: <a href="tel:+004122907716">+00 41 2290 7716</a> · Email: <a href="mailto:stay@makibafarm.example">stay@makibafarm.example</a> · Booking desk daily 08:00–19:00.',
	'kde6dc192' => 'Dairy farm since',
	'kde738676' => 'Fork hay',
	'kdf4f333c' => 'Book a stay →',
	'ke088b114' => 'Ilse Ferreira replies within 24 hours with details and a link for the 30% deposit.',
	'ke10b96f1' => '2 families, 6 guests',
	'ke211fff5' => 'To receive our seasonal letter, provide your email address in the subscription box or email stay@makibafarm.example with the subject line \'Farm letter request\'. Submitting your address opens your email application so you can send your request directly to our desk. We respect your inbox and never send promotional noise or share your details with third parties. You will receive only our four calm dispatches throughout the year, keeping you connected to Larkfield Hollow Farm.',
	'ke5ae3130' => 'Evening barbecue in the yard under the walnut tree (Tue, Thu, Sat).',
	'ke7143c92' => 'Arrive',
	'ke82fcefb' => 'Bottle-feed the calves',
	'ke8989221' => 'adult / child (4–12)',
	'ke89974a5' => 'Can children take part in the daily farm chores?',
	'ke9c877e4' => 'Baskets and milking aprons for the children.',
	'kead80e62' => 'Phone: <a href="tel:+004122907716">+00 41 2290 7716</a>',
	'keb39e6b3' => 'An adult beside under-8s',
	'kec86d6e0' => 'Check-in',
	'ked8968b4' => 'Noor Haddad',
	'kedfd56b3' => 'Check-out',
	'kee2452e8' => 'Meadow picnic',
	'kee4a4cd9' => '€210 per night, breakfast included',
	'kee7877fa' => 'Our herd is made up of 48 milking cows, primarily robust crosses of Holstein and Brown Swiss breeds chosen for their gentle temperament and rich milk. Herd manager Noor Haddad oversees animal welfare, monitoring each cow\'s health and guiding the daily parlour routines alongside Tomas Ferreira. From April through October, the herd spends its days grazing across seventy hectares of clover and ryegrass hill pasture. The cows walk up the lane each morning and return quietly in the late afternoon. Their fresh, wholesome milk goes directly to Lukas in the dairy room and to our breakfast table.',
	'keff0d3aa' => 'Herd manager',
	'kf02b55d5' => 'Fork down fresh, fragrant meadow hay from the barn loft.',
	'kf06c2e6c' => 'Seasonal notes and everyday observations from the barn, dairy, and fields.',
	'kf1106180' => 'Morning milk bottles in the straw pens with Mateo.',
	'kf1b8e280' => 'Farm work takes place outdoors in all seasons, so practical clothing is essential. Guests should bring sturdy closed shoes or wellingtons, casual clothing that can take a splash of mud, and waterproof coats for damp mornings. We provide baskets and milking aprons for children during chores. Rainy weather never halts the routine at Larkfield Hollow Farm. On wet days, milking continues under the dry roof of the parlour, chores move inside the calf barn, and butter making and bread baking take place warmly within the kitchen and dairy room.',
	'kf2265d0f' => 'Breakfast',
	'kf2577075' => 'Always, in every working area.',
	'kf74d08d0' => 'Farm Breakfast and Meadow Picnics',
	'kf86c0d36' => 'We invite children and parents to experience genuine agricultural chores alongside our family and farm staff. Participation is guided with care, ensuring that every activity is safe, educational, and fun for all ages.',
	'kf928ca12' => 'Our postal address is Larkfield Hollow Farm, 14 Weald Lane, Larkfield Valley. We are open for staying guests from 1 February through 20 December each year, with check-in from 15:00 to 18:00. If you are arriving by train at Larkfield railway station and require transport, please arrange a pick-up with Ilse prior to your journey. We look forward to welcoming you to the parlour, meadows, and barn.',
	'kfacc67eb' => 'Every room rate includes our complete farm breakfast served at 07:00 in the barn kitchen, featuring fresh milk, freshly churned butter, farm eggs, and oven-baked bread. All core farm activities—including the 05:30 morning milking, the 10:00 calf feeding and egg collection, and the 13:00 butter-making session with Lukas Brandt—are completely included for every guest. Our evening barbecue under the walnut tree is optional at €22 per adult and €11 per child.',
	'kfb27fa77' => 'Booking a stay is simple, personal, and handled directly with our family.',
	'kfc354b49' => 'above the hay barn',
